Bandit Level 13 - Level 14

Challenge: Use the provided SSH private key to log in as bandit14 and retrieve the password for the next level.

Solution

While logged in as bandit13, check that the private key exists:

ls

Output:

sshkey.private

Exit the Bandit server to return to your local machine:

exit

Copy the private key from the Bandit server to my local machine using scp:

scp -P 2220 bandit13@bandit.labs.overthewire.org:sshkey.private .
-P 2220 specifies the SSH port.
: separates the remote server from the file path.
. saved the file in my current local directory.

Changed the file permissions so only I can access the key:

chmod 700 sshkey.private

This changes the permissions from:

-rw-r-----

to:

-rwx------

Use the private key to log in as bandit14:

ssh -i sshkey.private bandit14@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220

Once logged in, read the password:

cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit14

Password: aaWecNkG4FhxJQxz07uiwzVP6bJiYS65

Explanation

scp securely copies the private key from the Bandit server to your local machine.
chmod 700 restricts access to the key so SSH will accept it.
ssh -i logs in using the private key instead of a password.

What I learned

scp transfers files securely between local and remote machines over SSH.
SSH can authenticate with a private key instead of a password.
Private keys must have restrictive permissions before SSH will use them.
